          "name": "catchEventHandlerExceptions",
          "description": "<p>By default, if an event handler throws an exception, the error propagates up the stack and the\napplication state is undefined. Code which follows the event handler will <em>not</em> be executed.</p>\n<p>Set this to <code>true</code> to catch exceptions thrown by this object's event handlers and continue processing the event.\nThe exception will be rethrown on a zero millisecond timeout, so it will not destroy the stack.</p>",
